  "id": "COMPOUND:21827 - PROTEIN:5865",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a mechanistic link between (+)-(8S,8'R)-4-hydroxy-3,3',4',5'-tetramethoxylignan and SK-VLB, through the target Microtubule-associated protein 1B. This compound appears to inhibit the activity of multiple downstream targets, including [(3aR,4S,6R,6aR,9aR,9bR)-6-hydroxy-6,9-dimethyl-3-methylidene-2-oxo-4,5,6a,7,9a,9b-hexahydro-3aH-azuleno[4,5-b]furan-4-yl] (E)-2-methylbut-2-enoate, 5,7-Dihydroxy-8-(3-Methylbutanoyl)-6-(3-Methylbut-2-Enyl)-4-Propylchromen-2-One, and Dendridine A. These targets are all implicated in the regulation of SK-VLB, suggesting a common pathway of action. The consistent presence of Microtubule-associated protein 1B as a target across multiple pathways supports a role for this compound in modulating SK-VLB activity. The evidence is robust and aligns with known mechanisms of action, though the exact molecular mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
